# Tool Input Validation

| Field  | Value                |
| ------ | -------------------- |
| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
| Status | Draft                |

This specification defines the registry boundary that rejects malformed model input before a tool executor can act on it.

## Contract

1. `ToolRegistry.execute` rejects missing required properties, wrong declared types and disallowed enum values with an actionable `ToolResponse.result` naming the property path and constraint, without executing the tool or disclosing input values in the result or logs; valid inputs including unknown properties pass through unchanged exactly once, without coercion or defaults, and an unknown tool still throws `Unknown tool: <name>`.
2. Registration compiles a static schema once, rejects an uncompilable schema immediately with the tool name, and reuses the compiled schema across subsequent executions.
3. A function-valued definition resolves its current schema on each execution and validates against it, caching compilation by resolved schema object identity rather than by tool name.

## Integration and delivery

The execution contract returns validation failures to the model as tool results, allowing a corrected retry within the existing five-round budget rather than raising a transport error.
The one-line comment on `execute` points here for its rejection-result and unknown-name-exception contract.
The validator belongs in runtime dependencies; README.md, docs/adding-a-tool.md and .specify/spec.md describe enforced input validation, unchanged unknown properties and bounded retries.
The release includes a MINOR version bump and a consumer-facing changelog and migration note explaining that executors no longer receive malformed input.
